*> vybe-test: cobol/alphabet_clause/alphabet_clause_alphanumeric_mix_runtime
*> origin: languages/cobol/tests/cobol/test_alphabet_clause.rs

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ALPHA20.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
SPECIAL-NAMES.
    ALPHABET MIXED-ALPHA IS "0" THRU "9" "A" THRU "Z".
    COLLATING SEQUENCE IS MIXED-ALPHA.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-VYBE-L PIC X(256).
01 DIGIT  PIC X VALUE "8".
01 LETTER PIC X VALUE "A".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    IF DIGIT < LETTER
        DISPLAY "MIXED-ORDER"
    END-IF.
    MOVE SPACES TO WS-VYBE-L
    STRING "MIXED-ORDER" DELIMITED SIZE INTO WS-VYBE-L
    IF WS-VYBE-L NOT = "MIXED-ORDER"
        DISPLAY "FAIL: want [MIXED-ORDER] got [" WS-VYBE-L "]"
        MOVE 1 TO RETURN-CODE
        RAISE EXCEPTION EC-PROGRAM
    END-IF.
    STOP RUN.

